From 0d531df727e2aee39e8ba50c0a86f46a0292095c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rafe Walker <45343084+rafe-walker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 13:55:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 09/17] feat(mcp): keep exec text consistent when skills cannot
 be loaded

Where the learn capability is off (self-hosted and any client the
feature flag does not include), the server still told the agent to
"Prioritize skills over tools" and tool text required skills it had no
way to load (P10: 3 of 8 guesses in the friction session). The exec
description sent dashboards to dashboard-widgets-batch-add, whose
widget_type enum has no insight tiles (P11). And query schemas carried
PostHog AI planner wording such as "the properties the user has provided
in the plan" (P14, 91 occurrences).

- The compact instructions say "Prioritize skills over tools." only when
  skills are enabled.
- With skills unavailable, exec drops "load the <name> skill" steps from
  info descriptions, schema field descriptions and _agentNotes, keeping
  whatever else the sentence asked for.
- The artifact guidance names insight-create with dashboards: [id] for
  insight tiles.
- Planner wording is rewritten where exec hands a schema to an agent
  (info, schema, validation errors); the frontend schema source and the
  generated wrappers are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
